From b89c1c985164f40a25fdcc2ff1d02098e157406d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:01:53 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: a50_firstlight: enable high-resolution timers

The ABOX driver sleeps usleep_range(10, 100) after each queued IPC
message. Without CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS the sleep rounds up to a full
tick (4 ms at HZ=250), so the audio DSP firmware received a burst of
stream-start messages ~75 ms late, one per tick (M10.3 B2b2 firmware
log), and the TFA9872 speaker-protection message raced the firmware's
library start. The stock 4.14 kernel and gki_defconfig both enable
high-resolution timers; CPU idle is disabled, so the arch timer never
stops.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I2ad26968c65e279ac08ce7856b18ce8ac0d5502c
---
 arch/arm64/configs/a50_firstlight_defconfig | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/a50_firstlight_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/a50_firstlight_defconfig
index 703f4f250..80d970ca7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/a50_firstlight_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/a50_firstlight_defconfig
@@ -140,3 +140,6 @@ CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD=y
 CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_TRANSIENT=y
+# ABOX IPC queue sleeps usleep_range(10, 100) between messages; without high-resolution timers each
+# sleep lasts a full tick (4 ms at HZ=250), delaying the audio DSP by tens of ms (stock and GKI: y).
+CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y
-- 
2.56.1

